# caravan_deem_witness.rish -- Caravan deem witness.
#
# `refer.rye` opened the last door: a quarrel old enough to count is put before a
# hand that is neither party to it, three facts copied off the wire onto a desk
# outside the argument. So the case travels at last -- and then nothing comes
# home, because nothing in the arc asks what that hand made of it.
#
#   THE HAND A CASE WENT TO IS READ BACK, AND ITS FINDING PUBLISHED.
#
# WHAT THIS RUNG PROVES, MEASURED:
#
#   * THE NUMBER THE TWO PLANS DISAGREE ON IS CASES CARRIED OUT THAT NOBODY IS
#     EVER HEARD BACK ON. Both runs carry the same case to the same desk, and the
#     hand at that desk has already written the same answer into their own box
#     for both. What parts them is whether the plan ever reads it. It falls from
#     1 to 0.
#   * THE FINDING IS READ OFF THE WIRE, NEVER WRITTEN BY A RUN. A supervisor able
#     to author the word against it has graded its own objection, which is the
#     whole thing the referring below existed to prevent. `DeemSilent` refuses by
#     name where the box holds nothing at all -- and a run under a silent desk
#     leaves the case honestly waiting rather than supplying a verdict.
#   * A FINDING MUST NAME THE CASE IT ANSWERS. `DeemMismatched` is the rung
#     itself, refused by name on metal: a desk that has heard this argument
#     before may still hold the answer to an older case, and publishing that
#     beside today's outcome puts a third hand's name on a word they never said
#     about this work.
#   * A FINDING CARRIES FOUR BYTES -- the three that named the case, echoed back
#     exactly as they were sent, and one more saying what the hand made of it.
#     A verdict with no argument attached could be filed beside any quarrel.
#   * A FINDING BELONGS TO THE HAND THAT WROTE IT -- proven as its own fold. It
#     survives a provisioning of this plan, and taking down the plan's own
#     published copy never reaches onto somebody else's desk to unsay what they
#     said. A supervisor able to edit the answer it quotes would be grading the
#     objection against it after all.
#   * THE READING IS THE LAST ACT OF THE RUN, after the referring below it,
#     because the case a finding is weighed against is the case that referring
#     just carried -- and because a run that carried nothing out is owed no
#     answer by anybody.
#   * A WORD FROM OUTSIDE CARRIES, AND NEVER DECIDES. Both runs settle `carried
#     out whole`, both leave the quarrel standing where its holder left it, both
#     leave the age at 4 and the standing loud, both leave the same case on the
#     desk, and both keep the word standing under it. A finding for the reader
#     changes what an operator knows about the argument, and nothing else.
#   * THE PRICE IS ONE BYTE BESIDE THE OUTCOME, AT NO COST IN WORK AT ALL. Both
#     runs take up 6 phases, absorb 3 into standing dependents, lose 3 arcs, take
#     the same judgment back, re-seat the same 3 phases, spend the same 6
#     dependents, post and carry the same correction, read the same reply, record
#     the same disagreement, escort the same published word, ask the same reader,
#     stand the same mark, tell the same raiser, carry the same position past
#     themselves, date it to the same age, publish the same standing, carry the
#     same case to the same third hand, and settle `carried`.
#   * FIVE REFUSALS THIS RUNG EARNS, matching the five below it. `DeemUnreferred`
#     is the moment an answer is taken at all. `DeemSilent` is whether one stands
#     on the wire to take. `DeemMismatched` is the whole point. `DeemMiscounted`
#     is the honesty of the count: every case carried out is answered or left
#     waiting, never both and never neither. `DeemMisrecorded` is the record,
#     read back from the one byte an operator opens.
#   * A RUN OWED NO WORD FROM ANYBODY PUBLISHES NONE, a plan nobody ever pressed
#     a quarrel against is answered by nobody, and a desk that has said nothing
#     yet leaves the case honestly waiting -- each proven on the wire rather than
#     only as a fold. A plan that loses nothing still reads as the line handed,
#     all 16 pairs, this arc's standing generalization test one tier further out.
#
# Six RED paths were proven on metal before this witness claimed GREEN. Skip the
# write and keep the read-back armed and the run refuses `DeemMisrecorded`. Read
# the desk as empty and the run refuses `DeemSilent`. Weigh the finding against a
# quarrel one run younger and the run refuses `DeemMismatched` -- the rung
# itself. Walk a run that carried nothing out into a reading and it refuses
# `DeemUnreferred`, which takes disarming the honest early return first, since
# that return catches it before the run can. Count one case as both answered and
# waiting and it refuses `DeemMiscounted`. Disarm every guard at once -- the
# write skipped, the read-back dropped, and the harness read of the note replaced
# by the answer it hoped for -- and the selftest calls itself GREEN while
# `caravan/.deems/plan.deem` does not exist at all, so an operator would believe
# a hand outside the argument had spoken to them. Seeing that once is what makes
# the reading back a check rather than decoration.
#
# Checks read the selftest output natively (`contains`), never a shell grep over
# interpolated output -- REDS %76 / %85, the apostrophe loom.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/caravan_deem_witness.rish

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "caravan/bin/deem"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p caravan/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build caravan/deem.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]

assert build.ok else "caravan deem build failed -- ${build.err}"

# The reader this witness runs is built here rather than borrowed (REDS %92).
let read_bin_build = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build caravan/read.rye -femit-bin=caravan/bin/read"]
assert read_bin_build.ok else "caravan read build failed -- ${read_bin_build.err}"

# The board declaration the rungs below opened, unchanged.
let published = run ["sh" "-c" "caravan/bin/read caravan/systems/serial_three_clients_board.bron 2>&1"]
assert published.ok else "the board declaration could not be read"
assert published.out contains "domains 4 -- channels 3 -- regions 11 -- grants 22" else "the board declaration changed shape"
assert published.out contains "verdict: whole" else "the board declaration did not read whole"

# A fresh start for the stores, the doorbells, this plan's notes, and the boxes
# outside it. Every quarrel and every finding this witness reads was seated by
# the lap itself, standing in for the hands that met this argument before today.
let clean = run ["sh" "-c" "rm -rf caravan/.regions caravan/.channels caravan/.deems caravan/.readers"]
assert clean.ok else "the region stores, doorbells, notes, and outside boxes could not be cleared"

let test = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert test.ok else "caravan deem selftest exited non-zero"
assert test.out contains "GREEN" else "caravan deem selftest not GREEN"
assert test.out contains "the hand the case went to is read back, and its finding published" else "the deem finding did not close"

# The reading and its five refusals, read straight, before any dependent runs.
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: unreferred, silent, mismatched, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the five deem refusals did not stand"
assert test.out contains "a case carried out is never heard from again" else "a bare plan did not read as one"
assert test.out contains "a finding carries four bytes: the case it answers, and the word on it" else "a finding did not name what it carries"
assert test.out contains "a hand outside the argument finds for the reader who objected" else "a finding for the reader did not read as one"
assert test.out contains "a hand outside the argument finds for the plan's own word" else "a finding for the plan did not read as one"

# The property that makes a finding worth reading, proven as its own fold: it
# belongs to the hand that wrote it, survives a provisioning of this plan, and
# is never taken back by a plan clearing its own copy.
assert test.out contains "a finding survives a provisioning, and belongs to the hand that wrote it" else "a finding was never proven past a provisioning"

# The three endings this rung reaches by publishing nothing, each on the wire.
assert test.out contains "a run owed no word from anybody publishes none" else "a plan that carried no case out published a finding"
assert test.out contains "a plan nobody ever pressed a quarrel against is answered by nobody" else "a plan nobody pressed was answered all the same"
assert test.out contains "a desk that has said nothing yet leaves the case honestly waiting" else "a silent desk did not leave the case waiting"

# The referring below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "a long-standing quarrel is put before a hand that is neither party" else "the referring below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a case survives a provisioning, and outlives the quarrel it was built from" else "a case was never proven past a provisioning"
assert test.out contains "five refusals stand by name: early, unaddressed, party, miscounted, misrecorded" else "the refer refusals stopped standing"

# The swelling below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether a long-standing quarrel reads where the outcome is read" else "the swelling below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a standing survives a provisioning, and falls with the quarrel it speaks for" else "a standing was never proven past a provisioning"

# The dwelling below it, unchanged and still weighed.
assert test.out contains "an age climbs by the run just stood and never shortens" else "the dwelling below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "an age survives a provisioning, and falls with the quarrel it counts" else "an age was never proven past a provisioning"

# The relenting, the heeding, the endurance, the appeal, the tidings, the
# standing, the term, the escort, the record, the hearing, the delivery, the
# amendment, the recantation, the bearing, and the mend below, unchanged.
assert test.out contains "a quarrel comes down on its holder's word and on nobody else's" else "the relenting below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it reads under the quarrel it inherited" else "the heeding below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether a pressed quarrel outlives the run that heard it" else "the endurance below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it reads what its reader says back" else "the appeal below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it writes back to the reader who objected" else "the tidings below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its marks carry the standing of their objection" else "the standing below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes how long the objection beside its word may stand" else "the term below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its word is read beside the reading against it" else "the escort below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its record may hold a disagreement" else "the record below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether it hears what its reader answers" else "the hearing below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its own corrections travel" else "the delivery below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its own corrections are addressed" else "the amendment below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan publishes whether its own judgments answer to a later run" else "the recantation below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a plan names what it expects of a phase, and what it would accept of a loss" else "the bearing below stopped being weighed"
assert test.out contains "a repair still refuses by name: unread, whole, overreaching" else "the mend below stopped being weighed"

# The generalization test the whole arc keeps.
assert test.out contains "a plan that loses nothing reads as the line handed, all 16 pairs" else "an unlost plan did not read as the line handed"

# The reading lap: one plan run twice over a case already sitting on a desk
# outside the argument, with that hand's own answer already in their box both
# times. Every number stands still -- the work, the dependents, the correction,
# the journey, the record, the escort, the asking, the mark, the telling, the
# reading back, the position carried forward, the word standing under it, the
# age, the standing, the case, the settlement -- and only the answer moves.
assert test.out contains "phases: 6 unread, 6 answered" else "the two plans ran different records"
assert test.out contains "dependents: 6 unread, 6 answered" else "reading a finding cost work it should not have"
assert test.out contains "phases absorbed into a standing dependent: 3 unread, 3 answered" else "the two plans absorbed different phases"
assert test.out contains "abandoned reach, conferred and never served: 3 unread, 3 answered" else "the two plans lost different work"
assert test.out contains "phases re-seated to carry what was lost: 3 unread, 3 answered" else "the two plans repaired different work"
assert test.out contains "standing judgments taken back on this run's own evidence: 1 unread, 1 answered" else "the recanting rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "readings corrected where they were read: 1 unread, 1 answered" else "the amending rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "corrections carried to the place their reader was reached: 1 unread, 1 answered" else "the couriering rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "disagreements written into the record: 1 unread, 1 answered" else "the disputing rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "published words standing beside the reading against them: 1 unread, 1 answered" else "the abiding rung stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "standing objections put back to the reader who raised them: 1 unread, 1 answered" else "the lapsing rung stopped asking under both plans"
assert test.out contains "marks carrying the standing of the objection they quote: 1 unread, 1 answered" else "the standing below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "raisers told how their own quarrel came out: 1 unread, 1 answered" else "the tidings below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "readers whose reply to the answer was read back: 1 unread, 1 answered" else "the appeal below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "positions carried past the run that heard them: 1 unread, 1 answered" else "a run whose reader still presses dropped their position"
assert test.out contains "inherited positions weighed into the run's own word: 1 unread, 1 answered" else "the regard stopped standing under a live quarrel"
assert test.out contains "standing positions let go on their holder's own word: 0 unread, 0 answered" else "a run closed a quarrel nobody had withdrawn"
assert test.out contains "standing positions left exactly where they were found: 1 unread, 1 answered" else "the relenting below stopped leaving the position standing"
assert test.out contains "standing positions this run said the age of: 1 unread, 1 answered" else "the dwelling below stopped dating under both plans"
assert test.out contains "standing quarrels whose note never said how long: 0 unread, 0 answered" else "a dating run left a standing quarrel undated"
assert test.out contains "standing quarrels published where the outcome is read: 1 unread, 1 answered" else "the swelling below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "long-standing quarrels an operator reads no louder than a fresh one: 0 against 0" else "a heralding run left a long-standing quarrel reading quietly"
assert test.out contains "long-standing quarrels carried to a hand that is neither party: 1 unread, 1 answered" else "the referring below stopped moving under both plans"
assert test.out contains "long-standing quarrels nobody outside the argument ever sees: 0 against 0" else "a referring run left a quarrel unheard outside"
assert test.out contains "carried cases whose answer was read and published: 0 unread, 1 answered" else "the reading did not part the two plans"
assert test.out contains "carried cases still waiting on a third hand's word: 1 unread, 0 answered" else "the other half of the count did not close"
assert test.out contains "cases carried out that nobody is ever heard back on: 1 against 0" else "the two plans left the same case unanswered"
assert test.out contains "work still standing when the supervisor exits: 0 unread, 0 answered" else "the two plans left different work standing"
assert test.out contains "the plan, as an operator finally reads it: carried out whole unread, carried out whole answered" else "a third hand's word decided what the work came to"
assert test.out contains "breaks a named turn: 0 unread, 0 answered" else "the reading run broke an order its author named"

# What an operator reads is what the wire carries, and what a hand outside the
# argument writes is what their own box carries. Every note is read here, outside
# the run that wrote it, exactly as each would be read by the person it was
# written for.
let settled = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.deems/plan.settled"]
assert settled.ok else "the plan published no settlement an operator could read"
assert settled.out contains "c" else "the wire did not carry the carried settlement the repair earned"

# The note this rung writes: one byte beside the settlement, in a word that is
# neither party's. The hand at the bench found for the reader who objected, and
# the plan still carried out whole -- which is the whole shape of a finding that
# carries and never decides.
let finding = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.deems/plan.deem"]
assert finding.ok else "the plan published no finding an operator could read"
assert finding.out contains "u" else "a finding for the reader was published as some other word"

# The hand that wrote it still holds their own word, in their own box, exactly as
# they wrote it -- the case echoed back and the verdict on the end of it.
let answer = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/bench.deem"]
assert answer.ok else "the hand outside the argument kept no answer of their own"
assert answer.out contains "cl" else "the finding did not echo the case it answers"

# The whole four bytes, read as numbers, since the age rides as a raw count
# rather than as a digit: 99 is `c` for carried, 108 is `l` for loud, 4 is the
# runs the quarrel has stood, and 117 is `u` for a finding for the reader.
let answer_bytes = run ["sh" "-c" "od -An -tu1 caravan/.readers/bench.deem | tr -s ' ' '-'"]
assert answer_bytes.ok else "the finding could not be read as bytes"
assert answer_bytes.out contains "-99-108-4-117" else "the finding did not echo the case, the age, and the word on it"

# The case below it, untouched by the answer taken from beside it.
let case = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/bench.case"]
assert case.ok else "no third hand was ever handed the case"
assert case.out contains "cl" else "a reading run rewrote the case it had already carried out"

# The forum, read by the run and never written by it.
let forum = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.deems/plan.forum"]
assert forum.ok else "the plan named no hand outside the argument at all"
assert forum.out contains "bench" else "the wire did not name the third hand this lap seated"

# And the reader who raised the quarrel wrote no finding, which is the arc.
let unspoken = run ["sh" "-c" "test -e caravan/.readers/desk.deem && echo present || echo absent"]
assert unspoken.ok else "the reader box could not be weighed"
assert unspoken.out contains "absent" else "a party to the argument wrote the finding on it"

# The standing below it, published beside the settlement and untouched here.
let standing = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.deems/plan.swell"]
assert standing.ok else "the standing note could not be read at all"
assert standing.out contains "l" else "a quarrel four runs old did not read as long-standing"

# The age below it, untouched by the reading taken from it.
let age = run ["sh" "-c" "od -An -tu1 caravan/.deems/plan.dwell | tr -d ' '"]
assert age.ok else "the age note could not be read at all"
assert age.out contains "4" else "a reading run rewrote the age it was only asked to read"

# The quarrel itself, untouched: a hand outside says what they make of it, and
# never whether it stands.
let quarrel_note = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.deems/plan.standing"]
assert quarrel_note.ok else "a reading run took down the position a third hand only weighed"
assert quarrel_note.out contains "p" else "the position standing over the plan changed under a reading run"

# The word standing under it, unchanged.
let regard = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.deems/plan.regard"]
assert regard.ok else "the regard note could not be read at all"
assert regard.out contains "u" else "an answered quarrel stopped standing over the plan's own word"

# The reader's own hand, in their own box, outside this plan's wire entirely --
# still pressing, which is exactly why their quarrel goes on standing.
let press = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.press"]
assert press.ok else "the reader replied nothing at all"
assert press.out contains "p" else "the holder of this lap's quarrel did not read as still pressing"

let plea = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.deems/plan.appeal"]
assert plea.ok else "the plan published no plea an operator could read"
assert plea.out contains "p" else "the record and the reader's own hand read differently"

let address = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.deems/plan.at"]
assert address.ok else "the plan kept no address for the reader who took its word"
assert address.out contains "desk" else "the wire did not name the place its reader was reached"

let beside = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.deems/plan.beside"]
assert beside.ok else "a run withdrew the mark its reader earned"
assert beside.out contains "s" else "the mark did not name the reading its reader holds"

let quarrel = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.deems/plan.dispute"]
assert quarrel.ok else "an open record kept no disagreement at all"
assert quarrel.out contains "cs" else "the record did not name the plan's reading and its reader's"

let correction = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.deems/plan.amend"]
assert correction.ok else "the plan published no correction an operator could read"
assert correction.out contains "bc" else "the wire did not name the two readings the correction stands between"

let box = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.told"]
assert box.ok else "the reader's own box was never written to"
assert box.out contains "bc" else "the reader's box did not carry the correction in the words they read"

let outof = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.readers/desk.outof"]
assert outof.ok else "the raiser of the quarrel was never told how it came out"
assert outof.out contains "t" else "a word that never moved was reported to its raiser as one that did"

let recant_note = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.deems/plan.recant"]
assert recant_note.ok else "the plan published no recantation an operator could read"
assert recant_note.out contains ".r...." else "the wire did not name the one judgment this run took back"

let lost_note = run ["sh" "-c" "cat caravan/.deems/plan.lost"]
assert lost_note.ok else "the plan published no loss an operator could read"
assert lost_note.out contains ".x.x.x" else "the wire did not name the three phases the plan lost"

# The dependents measure the loss in their own hands, exactly as the rungs below
# left them, and the follower that once spoke for the judgment falls with it.
assert test.out contains "falls as its author declared, holding 1 conferred arcs it never served" else "a falling dependent did not fall holding its conferral"
assert test.out contains "client_b: read 3 arcs of its own, 0 inherited at its first breath, 1 conferred, 0 returned, 1 still reachable at home" else "the dependent a conferral was made to did not read it as its own"
assert test.out contains "client_c: bytes differed" else "the follower that once spoke for the judgment came home after all"

say "GREEN: Caravan deem witness passed."
